# NAME: GoogleVoice
# AUTHOR: TEaPoT233
# VERSION: 0.1.0
# UPDATED: 2026-11-11
# FORMAT: Surge RULE-SET (not DOMAIN-SET)
# REPO: https://github.com/TEaPoT233/-/tree/main/rules/GoogleVoice
# RULES: 14
# No MITM required. Select your own policy when importing.
# Place this RULE-SET above general Google / proxy rules.
# Shared Google endpoints below also route traffic from other apps.
# Based on observed iOS API hosts and official Google documentation.
# Static validation only; end-to-end SMS, calls and push tests are pending.

# Google Voice web entry [S1]
DOMAIN,voice.google.com

# Voice API observed at https://www.googleapis.com/voice/...
# Shared host: ALL paths at www.googleapis.com will use this policy.
DOMAIN,www.googleapis.com

# Shared Google services observed during the iOS Voice session [O1].
# These are NOT exclusive to Voice. Host inclusion does not prove that
# every request in the capture was generated by Voice.
# Auth / account
DOMAIN,oauth2.googleapis.com
DOMAIN,oauthaccountmanager.googleapis.com
DOMAIN,accountcapabilities-pa.googleapis.com
# Contacts (people-pa had MITM failures; attribution is not confirmed)
DOMAIN,people-pa.googleapis.com
DOMAIN,peoplestack-pa.googleapis.com
# Notifications / avatar
DOMAIN,notifications-pa.googleapis.com
DOMAIN,lh3.googleusercontent.com

# Google-documented connectivity destinations [S2].
# telephony.goog and STUN can be shared with other services.
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,telephony.goog
DOMAIN,stun.l.google.com

# Google Workspace Voice media ranges [S2].
# Not a complete or verified range list for personal Google Voice.
# no-resolve avoids forcing DNS lookups for unrelated hostnames.
IP-CIDR,74.125.39.0/24,no-resolve
IP-CIDR6,2001:4860:4864:2::/64,no-resolve
# Documented STUN address; not an exclusive Voice identifier.
IP-CIDR,74.125.250.129/32,no-resolve

# References and scope: README.md in this directory.
# S1: https://support.google.com/voice/answer/10063441?hl=en
# S2: https://knowledge.workspace.google.com/admin/voice/voice-connectivity-requirements
# O1: 2026-11-11 iOS request observations; no raw capture is published.
